{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unverified-trigonous-flounder","creation_channel":"cli","description":"LIVE-proven (Bedrock us-east-1, haiku-4.5, exp_e/exp_f in /tmp/gate-experiments): build_agent_kwargs (agent_call.py:64-75) rewrites toolsets to .filtered(run_step <= limit). When the filter trips after any tool call, pydantic-ai omits tools/toolConfig from the next request while history still contains toolUse blocks; Bedrock Converse rejects it — ValidationException 400 'The toolConfig field must be defined when using toolUse and toolResult content blocks.' Anthropic direct has the equivalent documented constraint, and pydantic_ai maps tool_choice='none' on Bedrock to omitting toolConfig entirely (same 400). So the cutoff NEVER lands a run that has already made a tool call — it converts it into a provider error, which interpret_failure then reports as an outage.\n\nBlast radius: every armed site. completion_recovery.py:471 passes tool_step_limit=16 (_EVIDENCE_TOOL_STEPS) — the bounded-recovery fallback itself dies with the same 400 if an evidence run reaches step 17.\n\nWhy tests miss it: test_agent_call_seam.py / test_runner_pydantic_budget.py drive the cutoff with FunctionModel, which accepts a tools-less request over a tool_use history; the provider protocol constraint is unrepresented offline.\n\nFIX (part of c827's proposal): replace the empty-filter landing with synthetic tool-result steering (WrapperToolset returns a steering notice instead of executing; tools stay defined — LIVE-proven to land cleanly, exp_g/exp_h), and add a regression test asserting requests never omit tool definitions while history holds tool_use blocks.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n1. No code path empties the advertised tool surface mid-run after a tool call has occurred (agent_call.py cutoff removed or replaced by steering; completion_recovery.py:471 included).\n2. A regression test fails if any request would omit tools/toolConfig while message history contains tool_use blocks.\n3. A runaway or budget-tripped run on Bedrock/Anthropic lands with a parseable verdict instead of ModelHTTPError 400.","id":"e1b1-859e-a7b4-48f2","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"tool_step_limit empty-filter cutoff 400s on Bedrock/Anthropic — forced landing is provider-broken"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785953438954674001,"uuid":"18e6ad24-b7b6-485c-9aed-8e6bd95af07a"}